## Upstream bug worked around

Both `dsh-tool-pwsh-safe@0.1.1` and `powershell-fix@0.1.0` call
`ctx.shell.run(ctx.shell.resolve(...))`. The DSH 0.2.x shell seam exposes only
`resolve()` + `execute()` + `handle.result()`; `run()` does not exist, so both
upstream plugins fail at runtime with `ctx.shell.run is not a function`.
This package uses the correct seam.
